# Part 2: which camera budget a scene reaches first, 3840x2160
-- z^2 cells4 as stroked rows: 731 vectors, 536554 segments, by the budget01 demand
1 curve(s) a segment: 704 bytes x 536554 = 360 MiB, about 16 MiB of bins, 536554 curves against 4194304
2 curve(s) a segment: 952 bytes x 536554 = 487 MiB, about 33 MiB of bins, 1073108 curves against 4194304
4 curve(s) a segment: 1448 bytes x 536554 = 741 MiB, about 66 MiB of bins, 2146216 curves against 4194304
which row is real depends on perspective: a segment splits until it is within 1/256 px; that count is unmeasured
fill, if any, adds at least 72 + 2 x 168 + 48 = 456 bytes a segment
-- plan clone, once per camera frame in flight, outside every budget
1 generation(s) of segments: 45 MiB a frame before styles and shapes
2 generation(s) of segments: 90 MiB a frame before styles and shapes
